#show: template

#taxon[Lemma]
// #title[Title]

Let $f : X -> Y$ be a surjection. We define
$
  K(x,y) :-= (f(x) = f(y)).
$
Then $f$ induces an equivalence
$
  X slash K ~= Y, .. [x] |-> f(x).
$
Furthermore the quorient map $q : X -> X/K$ is surjective and we have an equality of propositions
$
  (q(x) = q(y)) <-> K(x,y)
$

